# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-1 and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch that holds them. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the classes, the minutes, the read rules and the NO-GO rules. Push ONE tag at a time and wait for its run to finish (the workflow keeps one pending run; queued tags are cancelled). Never cancel a running card job.
# B0 (STOP): the governor image. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefill-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag this build makes from the pushed tp4/prefill-1 head (sed -i 's/tp4-prefill-1/<tag>/' AD-*.env Z-reset.env). The adaptive Lever N
# governor (docs/lever-n-adaptive-governor.md) is image code (levern_policy, levern_scheduler, serving_prefill_admission): the jobs that run the twin need THIS image, and a commit of any file the image carries needs a new build and
# a new tag in every template that names it. With QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_ADAPTIVE unset the image decides, logs and paces exactly as tp4-next2-1 does (a test holds the whole log byte for byte), so the production-profile arms A1 and A2
# of the ABAB run on it too. The SHIP profile is baked as the serving default and the session cap 8 as max-num-seqs, the same default production runs, so the image could serve; refused by c2_serving_job.read_bake while the
# profile's owner_traffic_waiver decision is not APPROVED. READ: 'baking the serving default c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic with a session cap of 8', the provenance report with no problem line, the image id.
# A build, not a card job: it may run while the cards serve, never during a timing job. Duration (estimate): 40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefill-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
